{"name":"Sweater Weather","hex":"#ccccc5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweater weather","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A crisp, cool outdoor temperature that is warm enough to avoid a heavy winter coat, but chilly enough to comfortably wear a sweater."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweater_weather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweater Weather","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweater Weather\" is a song by American alternative band the Neighbourhood. The song was written by group members Jesse Rutherford, Zach Abels and Jeremy Freedman, and was produced by Justyn Pilbrow. It serves as the lead single from their debut studio album, I Love You (2013). \"Sweater Weather\" reached number one on the Billboard Alternative Airplay chart in June 2013, logging 11 non-consecutive weeks at the summit of the chart. Pentatonix covered the song for their 2018 album Christmas Is Here! with an accompanying music video. The song was also covered by Kurt Hugo Schneider, Alyson Stoner, and Max S in 2014."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Sweater_Weather_%28The_Neighborhood_single_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweater_Weather"},{"title":"Sweater","blocks":[{"text":"A sweater or pullover, also called a jersey or jumper, is a piece of clothing, typically with long sleeves, made of knitted or crocheted material that covers the upper part of the body. When sleeveless, the garment is often called a slipover, tank top, or sweater vest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Selburose-sweater.jpg/330px-Selburose-sweater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweater"},{"title":"Weather","blocks":[{"text":"Weather is the state of the Earth's atmosphere at a specific place and time, typically described in terms of temperature, humidity, cloud cover, and stability. On Earth, most weather phenomena occur in the lowest layer of the planet's atmosphere, the troposphere, just below the stratosphere. Weather refers to day-to-day temperature, precipitation, and other atmospheric conditions, whereas climate is the term for the averaging of atmospheric conditions over longer periods of time. When used without qualification, \"weather\" is generally understood to mean the weather of Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg/330px-Port_and_lighthouse_overnight_storm_with_lightning_in_Port-la-Nouvelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Hot_dog_sweater_1434172037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Hot_dog_sweater_1434172037.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"\"Hot dog\" sweater","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHot_dog_sweater_1434172037.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Jersei-coll-alt.jpg/500px-Jersei-coll-alt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Jersei-coll-alt.jpg/500px-Jersei-coll-alt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turtleneck sweater","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJersei-coll-alt.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/1940_Trachtenstrickjacke_anagoria.JPG/500px-1940_Trachtenstrickjacke_anagoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum